  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Wednesday 15 January 1908, for the places of Dr J. M. Moore, Edward Lunn, John McNally, J.P., Robert Thompson and C. W. Neill. Seven went to the poll: four retiring members, William Miller (a former member), Murtagh McCann, sen., and Hugh O'Hanlon. Declared at 9.30 p.m.; \"There was only one spoiled ballot paper.\" The electorate is not given; the Lurgan Mail of 20 January 1912 (p. 5) gives 804 as the number who polled. No party labels printed."
